153 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 635 0 R
/E (The book looks healthy, but its price no longer tracks risk. A $15B, 2.2 million life book, diversified across every industry, region and account size, sits at 88.7% MLR, only 3.7 points over its ceiling. Yet premium per life is almost flat, 1.3x across the book, while claims climb 16x with risk, so the healthy are overcharged and the high risk run underwater.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
154 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 636 0 R
/E (We reprice each account off a single lever, the renewal quote. Maximising book contribution hands every account one rate that covers its claims and marks up how captive it is, while staying inside the 80% retention floor and the 85% MLR ceiling. The one input we estimate, how renewal responds to price, is calibrated and causal.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
